WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Carry the audited boundary. Start with the Season 3 audit: preserve history, inherit fields, and keep the next question separate from prior conclusions.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Name one research question. Ask a bounded question about one session, one source lens, and one decision—not a promise about direction.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Declare the source and horizon. Record symbol universe, session window, freshness, contract scope, and the data lens before opening a candidate.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:04:00.000
Lock the required fields. Identity, sequence, source, freshness, and invalidation are intake requirements, not optional annotations.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:05:00.000
Assign the research owner. Name the reviewer, packet maintainer, replay operator, and escalation path before the first row enters.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Open a controlled packet. Keep observed, inferred, contradicted, and unknown states separate so the next workflow remains challengeable.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:07:00.000
Freeze the next test. Future rows can test the question; the audited Season 3 history remains published and unchanged.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:08:00.000
Choose the symbol universe. Next: S4E02 · choose the correct symbol universe before Rank · Symbols concentrates attention.
